IMPORT prelude
IMPORT `ccc-core`

-- ccc20-part16-interpretation.l4 -- section 493 (definitions for Part XVI) and section 493.01 (indictable offence) of the Criminal Code
-- (Canada), R.S.C., 1985, c. C-46, layer 1: the law, objectively. Part XVI is "Compelling Appearance of Accused Before a Justice and Interim Release".
-- Source: a plain-text rendering, made by a converter script, of the Justice Laws Website consolidation (current to 2026-09-30); it is not the
-- official text and nothing here is claimed verified against the official text. The French equivalents in parentheses are quoted, not encoded.
-- How an answer reads: JUST TRUE; JUST FALSE (the text says no in its own words); NOTHING (not covered). A caller never turns NOTHING into FALSE.
-- Sections 493.1, 493.11 and 493.2 (the principle of restraint) are in ccc20-part16-principles.l4 because they call rules of the later sections.

§ `Section 493 -- Definitions for this Part`

-- "accused includes (a) a person to whom a peace officer has issued an appearance notice under section 497, and (b) a person arrested for a criminal offence".
-- "includes" keeps the list open, so a person who is neither is NOT COVERED, not "not an accused".
-- src:11036 | 493 In this Part,
-- src:11037 | accused includes
-- src:11038 | (a) a person to whom a peace officer has issued an appearance notice under section 497, and
-- src:11039 | (b) a person arrested for a criminal offence; (prévenu)
@ref s 493 "accused" (src:11036-11039)
GIVEN `a peace officer has issued the person an appearance notice under section 497` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the person was arrested for a criminal offence` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 493 the person is an accused within the definition` MEANS
    IF `a peace officer has issued the person an appearance notice under section 497` OR `the person was arrested for a criminal offence`
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE NOTHING   -- NOTHING-kind (includes): "accused includes"

-- "judge means (a) in Ontario, a judge of the superior court of criminal jurisdiction of the Province, (b) in Quebec, a judge of the superior court ... or three judges of the Court of
-- Quebec, (c) [Repealed], (d) in NS, NB, MB, BC, PEI, SK, AB and NL, a judge of the superior court of criminal jurisdiction of the Province, (e) in Yukon and the Northwest Territories, a judge of
-- the Supreme Court, and (f) in Nunavut, a judge of the Nunavut Court of Justice". Whether a person is a "judge of the superior court of criminal jurisdiction" is a fact taken from s 2 (the
-- caller says which office the person holds).
-- src:11041 | judge means
-- src:11042 | (a) in the Province of Ontario, a judge of the superior court of criminal jurisdiction of the Province,
-- src:11043 | (b) in the Province of Quebec, a judge of the superior court of criminal jurisdiction of the province or three judges of the Court of Quebec,
-- src:11044 | (c) [Repealed, 1992, c. 51, s. 37]
-- src:11045 | (d) in the Provinces of Nova Scotia, New Brunswick, Manitoba, British Columbia, Prince Edward Island, Saskatchewan, Alberta and Newfoundland and Labrador, a judge of the superior court of criminal jurisdiction of the Province,
-- src:11046 | (e) in Yukon and the Northwest Territories, a judge of the Supreme Court, and
-- src:11047 | (f) in Nunavut, a judge of the Nunavut Court of Justice; (juge)
@ref s 493 "judge" (src:11041-11047)
DECLARE `s 493 the office the person holds` IS ONE OF
    `s 493 a judge of the superior court of criminal jurisdiction of the province`    -- (a), (b), (d)
    `s 493 three judges of the Court of Quebec`                                       -- (b)
    `s 493 a judge of the Supreme Court`                                              -- (e)
    `s 493 a judge of the Nunavut Court of Justice`                                   -- (f)
    `s 493 an office that is none of those`

@ref s 493 "judge" (src:11041-11047)
GIVEN province IS A `Province or territory`
      office IS A `s 493 the office the person holds`
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 493 the person is a judge as defined in section 493` MEANS
    CONSIDER province
    WHEN Ontario THEN `s 493 ordinary province` office
    WHEN Quebec THEN
        IF office EQUALS `s 493 a judge of the superior court of criminal jurisdiction of the province` OR office EQUALS `s 493 three judges of the Court of Quebec`
        THEN JUST TRUE
        ELSE JUST FALSE   -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "(b) in the Province of Quebec, a judge of the superior court of criminal jurisdiction of the province or three judges of the Court of Quebec"
    WHEN `Nova Scotia` THEN `s 493 ordinary province` office
    WHEN `New Brunswick` THEN `s 493 ordinary province` office
    WHEN Manitoba THEN `s 493 ordinary province` office
    WHEN `British Columbia` THEN `s 493 ordinary province` office
    WHEN `Prince Edward Island` THEN `s 493 ordinary province` office
    WHEN Saskatchewan THEN `s 493 ordinary province` office
    WHEN Alberta THEN `s 493 ordinary province` office
    WHEN `Newfoundland and Labrador` THEN `s 493 ordinary province` office
    WHEN Yukon THEN `s 493 territory with a Supreme Court` office
    WHEN `Northwest Territories` THEN `s 493 territory with a Supreme Court` office
    WHEN Nunavut THEN
        IF office EQUALS `s 493 a judge of the Nunavut Court of Justice`
        THEN JUST TRUE
        ELSE JUST FALSE   -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "(f) in Nunavut, a judge of the Nunavut Court of Justice"

-- paragraphs (a) and (d): the same limb for Ontario and for the eight provinces named in (d): a judge of the superior court of criminal jurisdiction of the Province.
@ref s 493 "judge" (a), (d) (src:11042)
GIVEN office IS A `s 493 the office the person holds`
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 493 ordinary province` MEANS
    IF office EQUALS `s 493 a judge of the superior court of criminal jurisdiction of the province`
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE JUST FALSE   -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "(a) in the Province of Ontario, a judge of the superior court of criminal jurisdiction of the Province"

-- paragraph (e): Yukon and the Northwest Territories, a judge of the Supreme Court.
@ref s 493 "judge" (e) (src:11046)
GIVEN office IS A `s 493 the office the person holds`
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 493 territory with a Supreme Court` MEANS
    IF office EQUALS `s 493 a judge of the Supreme Court`
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE JUST FALSE   -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "(e) in Yukon and the Northwest Territories, a judge of the Supreme Court"

-- The seam answer PLAN.md section 6 asks of this part for s 2 "release order": "the maker of the order is a judge as defined in section 493": BOOLEAN. "judge means" is a closed
-- definition and the function above never answers NOTHING, so the BOOLEAN is its answer compared with JUST TRUE.
@ref s 493 "judge" (the seam of s 2 "release order") (src:11041-11047)
GIVEN province IS A `Province or territory`
      office IS A `s 493 the office the person holds`
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`s 493 the maker of the order is a judge as defined in section 493` MEANS
    `s 493 the person is a judge as defined in section 493` province office EQUALS JUST TRUE

-- "warrant, when used in relation to a warrant for the arrest of a person, means a warrant in Form 7 and, when used in relation to a warrant for the committal of a person, means a warrant in Form 8."
-- src:11053 | warrant, when used in relation to a warrant for the arrest of a person, means a warrant in Form 7 and, when used in relation to a warrant for the committal of a person, means a warrant in Form 8. (mandat)
@ref s 493 "warrant" (src:11053)
DECLARE `s 493 what the warrant is for` IS ONE OF
    `s 493 a warrant for the arrest of a person`
    `s 493 a warrant for the committal of a person`
    `s 493 a warrant for some other purpose`

@ref s 493 "warrant" (src:11053)
GIVEN purpose IS A `s 493 what the warrant is for`
      `the warrant is in Form 7` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the warrant is in Form 8` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 493 the document is a warrant within the definition` MEANS
    CONSIDER purpose
    WHEN `s 493 a warrant for the arrest of a person` THEN
        IF `the warrant is in Form 7` THEN JUST TRUE
        ELSE JUST FALSE   -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "means a warrant in Form 7"
    WHEN `s 493 a warrant for the committal of a person` THEN
        IF `the warrant is in Form 8` THEN JUST TRUE
        ELSE JUST FALSE   -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "means a warrant in Form 8"
    WHEN `s 493 a warrant for some other purpose` THEN NOTHING   -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "when used in relation to a warrant for the arrest of a person"

§ `Section 493.01 -- Clarification: indictable offence`

-- "a reference to an indictable offence includes an offence that may be punishable on summary conviction if it is also an offence that may be prosecuted by indictment, unless the prosecutor has
-- elected to proceed by way of summary conviction". Every test of "an indictable offence" in this range calls the function below, so this clarification is encoded once. The offence is
-- described by its class (a core type, answered by the part that owns the offence: PLAN.md seam R2) and by whether the prosecutor has elected summary conviction.
-- src:11054 | Clarification — indictable offence
-- src:11055 | 493.01 For greater certainty, a reference to an indictable offence includes an offence that may be punishable on summary conviction if it is also an offence that may be prosecuted by indictment, unless the prosecutor has elected to proceed by way of summary conviction.
@ref s 493.01 (src:11054-11055)
DECLARE `s 493.01 the offence charged` HAS
    `the class of the offence`                                                       IS A `Class of offence`
    `the prosecutor has elected to proceed by way of summary conviction`             IS A BOOLEAN

@ref s 493.01 (src:11055)
GIVEN offence IS A `s 493.01 the offence charged`
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 493.01 the reference to an indictable offence includes the offence` MEANS
    CONSIDER offence's `the class of the offence`
    WHEN `an indictable offence` THEN JUST TRUE
    WHEN `an offence punishable on summary conviction` THEN JUST FALSE   -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "if it is also an offence that may be prosecuted by indictment" (a summary-only offence is not also prosecutable by indictment)
    WHEN `an offence that the section makes both indictable and punishable on summary conviction` THEN
        IF offence's `the prosecutor has elected to proceed by way of summary conviction`
        THEN JUST FALSE   -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "unless the prosecutor has elected to proceed by way of summary conviction"
        ELSE JUST TRUE

-- The Boolean the later rules of this range use for "an indictable offence". The function above never answers NOTHING, so the comparison with JUST TRUE cannot turn a NOTHING into FALSE.
@ref s 493.01 (used by every later test of "an indictable offence") (src:11055)
GIVEN offence IS A `s 493.01 the offence charged`
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`s 493.01 the offence is treated as an indictable offence` MEANS
    `s 493.01 the reference to an indictable offence includes the offence` offence EQUALS JUST TRUE
